WEBVTT

00:01.950 --> 00:04.670
<i>I'm pretty decent at communicating.</i>

00:04.670 --> 00:07.100
<i>For me, as someone whose job 
it is to write about people,</i>

00:07.100 --> 00:09.270
<i>age and sex are just characteristics,</i>

00:09.270 --> 00:11.270
<i>so I've never perceived either as a barrier.</i>

00:11.360 --> 00:13.780
<b>Feels like he's totally getting stared at...</b>

00:11.360 --> 00:13.780
<b>Badump

Badump</b>

00:13.860 --> 00:15.280
<b>Uneasy</b>

00:15.610 --> 00:18.580
<b>Tends to drink something 
when he's in a tough spot.</b>

00:15.610 --> 00:18.580
<b>Gulp</b>

00:18.920 --> 00:23.210
<i>A seven-year age difference 
basically isn't a thing for me.</i>

00:23.210 --> 00:26.220
<i>So I thought we'd open up to 
each other by now, but still...</i>

00:27.170 --> 00:28.040
Hayate.

00:29.590 --> 00:31.150
That's my coffee.

00:31.050 --> 00:31.510
<b>Spit</b>

02:02.470 --> 02:06.980
<b>#22 
Summer Festival</b>

02:03.440 --> 02:04.990
I'm so sorry!

02:05.690 --> 02:06.540
It's fine.

02:06.540 --> 02:07.620
You can finish it.

02:07.620 --> 02:09.930
Indirectly kissing a guy is so lame.

02:09.930 --> 02:10.870
Huh?

02:10.870 --> 02:13.390
I guess you'd rather be indirectly 
kissing a girl, right?

02:13.710 --> 02:15.200
That makes sense.

02:15.200 --> 02:16.540
How does that make sense?!

02:16.540 --> 02:17.150
Are you stupid?

02:17.150 --> 02:17.780
You're dumb!

02:17.780 --> 02:18.650
Stupid! Stupid!

02:19.590 --> 02:21.140
Your small vocabulary is cute.

02:21.140 --> 02:24.020
Shun, I don't think you can 
ever win against Motoharu-kun.

02:24.490 --> 02:26.790
I really am sorry.

02:28.580 --> 02:30.330
Hayate, look at me.

02:30.710 --> 02:31.790
<b>Frozen</b>

02:31.180 --> 02:32.300
I can't.

02:32.300 --> 02:33.770
You've been nervous this whole time.

02:33.770 --> 02:35.800
You're so easy to read, Hayate-kun.

02:37.670 --> 02:40.140
<i>There's no reason to be so nervous, though.</i>

02:40.660 --> 02:44.010
<i>I wonder how far he'll get 
at today's summer festival.</i>

02:45.320 --> 02:47.550
Mima-san said he's leaving his office now.

02:47.550 --> 02:49.270
Then we should get going, too.

02:53.700 --> 02:55.800
I'm heading out now.

02:55.800 --> 02:56.820
See you tomorrow!

02:56.820 --> 02:58.420
Well, this is pretty rare.

02:58.420 --> 03:00.100
You're actually leaving on time.

03:00.100 --> 03:00.990
Yes.

03:00.990 --> 03:03.770
I was invited to the summer festival.

03:03.770 --> 03:05.290
The summer festival?

03:05.290 --> 03:06.500
With a girl?!

03:07.310 --> 03:08.700
They're all guys.

03:08.970 --> 03:10.770
Boring.

03:10.770 --> 03:12.950
I'll get ready to go home too.

03:12.950 --> 03:14.350
Ah, man.

03:14.350 --> 03:18.410
Well, I can't really imagine you 
on a date with a woman anyway.

03:18.660 --> 03:20.280
Souma-kun is going to be there too.

03:20.280 --> 03:23.640
Oh, yeah, he said he was going to eat 
dinner tonight at the food stalls.

03:23.640 --> 03:25.080
Would you like to join us?

03:25.080 --> 03:26.340
I'll pass.

03:26.340 --> 03:28.380
I'll have him bring something home for me.

03:28.610 --> 03:30.170
You don't have a festival every day.

03:30.170 --> 03:31.100
Have fun!

03:31.420 --> 03:32.160
All right.

03:33.030 --> 03:34.290
They have candied apples.

03:34.290 --> 03:35.430
And candied strawberries too!

03:35.430 --> 03:37.360
The sauces all smell so good.

03:37.360 --> 03:38.950
This is bordering on violence.

03:38.950 --> 03:39.950
I'm starving.

03:40.490 --> 03:42.750
It's not surprising, but 
this place is packed.

03:42.750 --> 03:44.400
You think we'll find Mima-san?

03:44.400 --> 03:47.020
He should be around here somewhere.

03:47.020 --> 03:48.070
There.

03:48.070 --> 03:49.620
It's good he's so tall.

03:51.110 --> 03:52.350
Good evening.

03:52.350 --> 03:53.570
Good evening!

03:53.570 --> 03:54.920
Have you been waiting long?

03:54.920 --> 03:57.010
Oh, not at al—

03:57.000 --> 04:01.720
<b>Tada</b>

03:57.530 --> 03:59.270
You're really part of the group, huh.

03:59.270 --> 04:00.120
Right?

04:00.120 --> 04:01.720
Though I'm the only one around 30.

04:02.480 --> 04:04.290
Did you get bit by a mosquito?

04:04.590 --> 04:08.900
Ah, yes, it does happen more 
often if you stand still.

04:08.900 --> 04:09.780
It's itchy.

04:10.010 --> 04:13.260
You don't seem like the type 
to get bitten by mosquitoes.

04:13.260 --> 04:14.700
No, I really...

04:15.150 --> 04:16.520
<b>Slap!!</b>

04:17.000 --> 04:17.730
<i>Huh?</i>

04:20.690 --> 04:21.900
<b>Mole</b>

04:22.190 --> 04:24.120
<i>Oh. That was a mole.</i>

04:24.390 --> 04:25.450
It was nothing.

04:25.450 --> 04:26.520
Shall we?

04:26.900 --> 04:27.780
Ouch.

04:28.140 --> 04:30.440
<i>I guess he's really sensitive 
to mosquitoes now.</i>

04:32.330 --> 04:34.530
Shun, they've got your omelet soba.

04:32.910 --> 04:39.550
<b>Omelet soba</b>

04:34.530 --> 04:35.460
I want some!

04:35.460 --> 04:36.620
Don't worry about it.

04:36.620 --> 04:38.340
You kids don't have to 
take out your wallets.

04:38.340 --> 04:39.550
<i>Kids?</i>

04:39.550 --> 04:40.890
You mean you're paying?

04:40.890 --> 04:41.940
What a god!

04:41.940 --> 04:42.880
Are you sure?

04:42.880 --> 04:44.510
Leave it to the adults.

04:44.940 --> 04:48.450
Takayuki, let's use rock-paper-scissors
 to decide who pays for each one.

04:48.450 --> 04:49.540
Sure.

04:50.850 --> 04:54.740
<i>Mima-san and Igarashi-sensei 
really were classmates, huh?</i>

04:51.380 --> 04:53.250
Rock, paper, scissors!

04:53.250 --> 04:54.750
Again!

04:54.740 --> 04:57.040
<i>It's so amazing that they're friends.</i>

04:55.050 --> 04:56.710
Again!

04:56.710 --> 04:57.820
I win!

04:57.820 --> 05:00.210
So that means you pay for this one, Takayuki!

05:00.210 --> 05:01.330
Got it.

05:01.710 --> 05:03.830
Shun-kun, how many portions do we need?

05:03.830 --> 05:05.000
Let me see...

05:05.000 --> 05:06.650
I'll help you carry them.

05:09.130 --> 05:11.240
We'll go get some takoyaki.

05:11.240 --> 05:12.030
Okay!

05:12.380 --> 05:13.850
Extra mayo on mine!

05:13.850 --> 05:14.740
Okay.

05:15.330 --> 05:16.070
Let's go.

05:16.070 --> 05:17.070
H-Huh?!

05:21.960 --> 05:24.770
Hayate, we'll get separated 
if you fall too far behind.

05:25.050 --> 05:26.980
I'm really sorry!

05:28.320 --> 05:30.790
No need to be nervous.

05:31.820 --> 05:34.640
I'm really happy to know 
you as one of my readers,

05:35.080 --> 05:37.920
but I'd also really like to get 
to know you as one of my friends.

05:39.880 --> 05:41.280
I'm really sorry.

05:41.280 --> 05:42.560
<i>I got rejected...</i>

05:42.910 --> 05:45.330
<i>Maybe I shouldn't push too much.</i>

05:45.330 --> 05:46.310
I...

05:47.270 --> 05:50.240
I really love your books!

05:51.720 --> 05:56.160
If I were to get involved 
in your day-to-day life,

05:56.160 --> 05:59.290
I might indirectly influence 
your inspiration somehow,

05:59.690 --> 06:03.500
and then it would not longer be a 
100% pure Igarashi Motoharu world!

06:03.820 --> 06:07.610
When I'm before you, 
I just want to be a rock.

06:08.470 --> 06:11.470
<b>A nerd who wants to be a</b>

06:08.470 --> 06:11.470
<b>rock before one of his gods</b>

06:11.830 --> 06:14.480
I can see you are a passionate reader.

06:15.720 --> 06:22.610
<b>Takoyaki</b>

06:16.030 --> 06:17.980
You don't have to worry about all that.

06:19.090 --> 06:21.160
Is this place okay for the takoyaki?

06:21.160 --> 06:22.610
Yes.

06:23.040 --> 06:26.760
Sorry for thinking I could 
actually do anything.

06:26.760 --> 06:28.290
I'm just a rock.

06:28.720 --> 06:30.600
That's not what I meant.

06:31.070 --> 06:33.590
I'll take four sets of six, please.

06:33.590 --> 06:35.150
One of them with extra mayo.

06:35.150 --> 06:35.830
Coming right up!

06:36.820 --> 06:41.290
The first protagonist I ever 
wrote was based off of Takayuki.

06:42.490 --> 06:45.320
I was excited about the work of remolding

06:45.320 --> 06:48.500
something I experienced in 
real life into something else.

06:48.940 --> 06:50.640
Whoever I meet,

06:50.640 --> 06:51.970
whatever I do,

06:52.280 --> 06:54.350
anything I've absorbed—

06:54.350 --> 06:57.590
it all becomes my own as 
soon as I put it on paper.

06:58.550 --> 07:01.460
So I want you to relax 
and stay as my reader,

07:01.460 --> 07:03.150
but I'd also like you to be my friend.

07:04.340 --> 07:05.640
<i>He's so cool...</i>

07:06.150 --> 07:07.110
<b>Bow</b>

07:06.180 --> 07:07.650
Thank you so much.

07:07.650 --> 07:09.120
And I'm sorry.

07:10.200 --> 07:12.430
And over time, you can 
stop holding back, too.

07:12.430 --> 07:15.330
Shall we go back and join the others?

07:15.330 --> 07:16.110
Right.

07:16.200 --> 07:18.910
<b>Takoyaki</b>

07:16.290 --> 07:18.950
Lads, your takoyaki!

07:20.310 --> 07:24.340
You know, after everything, your 
first book is still my favorite.

07:24.340 --> 07:25.320
Really?

07:25.320 --> 07:27.290
Then again, I can see why you'd like it.

07:27.560 --> 07:28.330
Yes!

07:28.330 --> 07:31.790
The marvelous interplay between the 
characters breeds such a peculiar atmosphere!

07:32.280 --> 07:35.140
What kind of books do you usually read?

07:35.140 --> 07:36.320
I read all sorts of things.

07:36.320 --> 07:37.470
Want to come over sometime?

07:37.470 --> 07:38.210
What?

07:38.210 --> 07:40.150
It'd be easier if I just 
showed you my bookshelves.

07:40.510 --> 07:43.490
<i>Suddenly they're like best buds.</i>

07:43.490 --> 07:44.600
<i>What happened?</i>

07:45.190 --> 07:47.820
<i>I'm pretty decent at communicating.</i>

07:48.450 --> 07:51.090
<i>For me, as someone whose job 
it is to write about people,</i>

07:48.460 --> 07:50.280
Mima-san, Igarashi-sensei,

07:50.280 --> 07:53.550
thank you so much for treating 
us to all this food.

07:51.090 --> 07:55.380
<i>the moment when he revealed what 
was in his heart made me happy.</i>

07:53.550 --> 07:55.180
Thank you so much!

07:55.180 --> 07:56.180
Don't mention it.

07:55.380 --> 07:59.230
<i>I feel like I got another piece of why 
understanding people is so fun.</i>

07:56.180 --> 07:57.650
Today was fun!

07:57.650 --> 07:59.270
One summer event checked off.

07:59.270 --> 08:02.330
Going to a summer festival with friends 
is such a teenager thing to do.

08:00.280 --> 08:02.690
<i>A certain man was the impetus,</i>

08:02.330 --> 08:03.930
You're around 30, though.

08:02.690 --> 08:04.380
<i>and now here I am.</i>

08:03.930 --> 08:06.490
Next year, we should come back in yukata.

08:05.550 --> 08:08.960
<i>In the end, it seems like 
this was the right choice.</i>

08:06.490 --> 08:08.910
Sounds like effort.

08:11.080 --> 08:13.060
All right, I have to go this way now.

08:13.060 --> 08:15.330
Oh, same for me.

08:15.330 --> 08:16.370
I see.

08:16.370 --> 08:18.300
Shun, are you going home, 
or back to the cafe?

08:18.300 --> 08:19.360
I'm going home.

08:19.360 --> 08:21.760
I'm going this way. See you next time.

08:21.760 --> 08:23.360
See you next time!

08:24.330 --> 08:26.060
So you're going this way, too.

08:26.060 --> 08:27.980
I'll be turning at the next corner.

08:27.980 --> 08:29.370
Me too.

08:29.950 --> 08:31.570
I guess we live close to each other.

08:31.570 --> 08:34.070
There's a lot of apartment 
buildings in this area.

08:37.630 --> 08:39.590
<i>I wonder how long we'll 
keep walking together.</i>

08:45.620 --> 08:47.520
This... this isn't what it looks like!

08:47.520 --> 08:50.870
I wasn't trying to scope out where you live!

08:50.870 --> 08:53.560
I'm a fan, but I would never stoop so low!

08:53.560 --> 08:56.210
Don't worry. I never 
suspected you of anything.

08:58.270 --> 09:00.780
Who would've thought we 
lived in the same building?

09:00.780 --> 09:02.050
That was unexpected.

09:03.260 --> 09:06.580
I'm home often, so you're welcome 
to come over whenever you like.

09:06.580 --> 09:07.200
Huh?

09:06.830 --> 09:08.230
<i>First floor.</i>

09:07.200 --> 09:08.230
No, I couldn't!

09:08.670 --> 09:09.730
I have a cat.

09:09.730 --> 09:11.110
A cat?

09:12.300 --> 09:13.940
That sounded like I'm 
luring you with the cat.

09:14.400 --> 09:15.830
You don't have to come over alone, either.

09:15.830 --> 09:18.730
You can call Takayuki or 
Souma or Shun over anytime.

09:18.730 --> 09:21.320
You can come sit around in the library, too.

09:23.490 --> 09:25.550
<i>Please select a floor.</i>

09:25.750 --> 09:26.460
<b>Oh</b>

09:27.060 --> 09:28.190
Which floor are you on?

09:28.190 --> 09:29.560
The sixth.

10:59.970 --> 11:04.970
<b>Summer Sky and Sea</b>

10:59.970 --> 11:04.980
<b>Coming up next</b>

11:04.980 --> 11:09.970
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>

11:04.980 --> 11:09.970
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>
